First of all: Job well done Mac development team.

Now a couple of comments and suggestions.

(1) It would be nice if the commands acted a little more closely to the
unix tty version. One thing I that I find consistently annoying me is when
selecting an item by inventory letter. For example to apply my

    N - blessed unicorn horn

when I cannot quite remember which letter it is.

Unix version: <a>pply, <?> to list items, space to continue, <N> to use it.
Mac version:  <a>pply, <?> to list items, space cancels, <N> runs!!! Arrgh!

(2) I *really* miss the <ESC> to skip rest of messages command, especially
when dropping all my stuff on an altar (or using ring of conflict in large
room of monsters). space...space...space...space...yawn...zzzzzz...zzzzzz

I'm very happy with the Mac nethack implementation. If these two (minor?)
points were addressed, I would be very very happy with it.

